WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.240
In this video, you add an SSH public key to SUSE Virtualization. Virtual machines that use the key let you log in without a password.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.380
In the navigation menu, expand Advanced,

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.730
and select SSH Keys.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.200
Select Create.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:26.140
Choose the namespace. Virtual machines in this namespace can use the key.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.260
Give the key a name.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:33.600
Paste the public key. You can also load it from a file with Read from File.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.050
Select Create.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.480
SUSE Virtualization validates the key and shows its fingerprint.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.930
To use the key, go to Virtual Machines

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.500
and select Create.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.540
In the same namespace,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:56.120
open the SSH key list on the Basics tab and pick the key.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:04.310
When the virtual machine starts, cloud-init adds this key to the default user's authorized keys.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:10.993
Your SSH key is stored and ready to use. Next, you create a Linux virtual machine.
